WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:00.834 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Welcome back.

00:00:00.834 --> 00:00:01.534 line:92%
-Thank you for having me.

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:03.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I am so happy to have you.
And congratulations.

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:05.872 align:start size:94% position:6%
You were nominated for
three Golden Globe awards,

00:00:05.872 --> 00:00:09.476
a couple for "Sharp Objects" --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:09.476 --> 00:00:10.810 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Thank you.

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:11.478 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-And one for "Vice."

00:00:11.478 --> 00:00:13.880 align:start size:94% position:6%
On a morning like that,
do you celebrate?

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:15.248 line:92%
Are you good at celebrating?

00:00:15.248 --> 00:00:17.250 line:92%
-I'm really bad at celebrating.

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:17.650 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Gotcha.

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:18.351 line:92%
-Or at appropriate times.

00:00:18.351 --> 00:00:20.653 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, I'll just like celebrate
a Tuesday night.

00:00:20.653 --> 00:00:24.624 size:84% position:42%
But -- no, I always get
a little uncomfortable

00:00:24.624 --> 00:00:28.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
having self celebrations,
me parties.

00:00:28.528 --> 00:00:30.363 line:92%
-Yeah. I guess that makes sense.

00:00:30.363 --> 00:00:33.466 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's a Muppet reference
for you guys.

00:00:33.466 --> 00:00:34.034 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:34.034 --> 00:00:36.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But that's very honest of you
to say.

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:40.473
-Yeah. I mean, I'm really
grateful and thrilled.

00:00:40.473 --> 00:00:42.208 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just -- yeah.
-Yeah.

00:00:42.208 --> 00:00:43.209 size:75% position:38% line:92%
I feel like -- yeah.

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:45.145 align:start size:94% position:6%
A celebration for
the nomination,

00:00:45.145 --> 00:00:47.914
that's just Jinx City, you know,
once you do that.

00:00:47.914 --> 00:00:51.317
This is -- Congratulations.
Such a fantastic portrayal.

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:54.421 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously you're playing
a real person, Lynne Cheney.

00:00:54.421 --> 00:00:55.789 line:92%
But I heard you also based it,

00:00:55.789 --> 00:00:58.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
not only on her,
but on your grandmother.

00:00:58.291 --> 00:00:59.225 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-On my grandmother.

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:00.393 line:92%
-How did you come to that?

00:01:00.393 --> 00:01:01.861 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, as I started
researching her,

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:04.864
there was something in her voice
and something that sort of

00:01:04.864 --> 00:01:06.633 size:75% position:38%
started to remind me
of my grandmother.

00:01:06.633 --> 00:01:09.269 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the more I did research --
my grandma is from Utah.

00:01:09.269 --> 00:01:12.138 align:start size:94% position:6%
I understand we have
some Utah folks here today.

00:01:12.138 --> 00:01:13.540 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:14.874 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Yeah.

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:17.177
There was just something
in the way she was raised.

00:01:17.177 --> 00:01:21.181 align:start size:94% position:6%
My grandmother
was raised on a farm.

00:01:21.181 --> 00:01:23.583 align:start size:94% position:6%
There was a pioneering spirit.
So, yeah.

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:27.187 line:92%
My grandma was -- she was tough.

00:01:27.187 --> 00:01:28.721 line:92%
Like, she told it how it was.

00:01:28.721 --> 00:01:30.123 line:92%
There was no sugar-coating it.

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:32.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is probably
why you don't celebrate.

00:01:32.859 --> 00:01:34.260 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:34.961 line:92%
Golden Globe nominations.

00:01:34.961 --> 00:01:36.629 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, I mean, when we would go
over to her house,

00:01:36.629 --> 00:01:39.365
and it was the idea that the
kids would help out, you know?

00:01:39.365 --> 00:01:41.501 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we would, like,
clean cans in the --

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:44.104 align:start size:94% position:6%
There was no, like,
Grandma spoiling you.

00:01:44.104 --> 00:01:45.972 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow!
-Which I was used to.

00:01:45.972 --> 00:01:46.739 size:88% position:44% line:92%
So I didn't know that --

00:01:46.739 --> 00:01:50.276
-After you cleaned a can,
what would you use it for?

00:01:50.276 --> 00:01:51.344 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.344 --> 00:01:52.479 line:92%
-You would put it back up

00:01:52.479 --> 00:01:55.148 align:start size:94% position:6%
with all the other cans
in the cupboard.

00:01:55.148 --> 00:01:57.150 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, no.
She was great, but tough.

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:59.652 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah. We did a lot of --
-A lot of chores?

00:01:59.652 --> 00:02:02.021 align:start size:94% position:6%
-A lot of chores.
-You got worked hard?

00:02:02.021 --> 00:02:04.757 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We got worked hard
at Grandma's house, yeah.

00:02:04.757 --> 00:02:07.193 size:75% position:38%
So I guess something
about the work ethic

00:02:07.193 --> 00:02:10.063 align:start size:94% position:6%
that was instilled
reminded me of Lynne Cheney.

00:02:10.063 --> 00:02:12.632 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And obviously a lot's being
talked about

00:02:12.632 --> 00:02:15.535
Christian Bale's transformation
into Dick Cheney.

00:02:15.535 --> 00:02:18.138 align:start size:94% position:6%
But you also had to
spend a ton of time

00:02:18.138 --> 00:02:20.039 align:start size:94% position:6%
in hair and makeup
for this role.

00:02:20.039 --> 00:02:22.976 align:start size:94% position:6%
How do you pass time when you
have one of these parts

00:02:22.976 --> 00:02:26.212 align:start size:94% position:6%
where you spend so much time
doing that element?

00:02:26.212 --> 00:02:27.147 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-I found different ways.

00:02:27.147 --> 00:02:30.483 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, we would -- Christian
often had headphones on.

00:02:30.483 --> 00:02:33.686
I would often sing
as Lynne Cheney, which was fun.

00:02:33.686 --> 00:02:37.223
-What sort of songs would
your Lynne Cheney sing?

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:39.058 line:92%
-Mostly hits from the '80s.

00:02:39.058 --> 00:02:39.492 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Okay.

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:40.660 line:92%
-Like "Pour Some Sugar on Me."

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:42.695 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Gotcha.
Now, this sounds like a song

00:02:42.695 --> 00:02:45.632 align:start size:94% position:6%
maybe Lynne Cheney
wouldn't be a fan of.

00:02:45.632 --> 00:02:46.199 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.199 --> 00:02:48.101 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don't think she would.
-Yeah.

00:02:48.101 --> 00:02:49.602 line:92%
-But it was fun. I would --

00:02:49.602 --> 00:02:52.772 line:92%
♪♪ Pour some sugar on me ♪♪

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:54.040 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
You know --

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:55.842 line:92%
♪♪ In the name of love ♪♪

00:02:55.842 --> 00:02:57.310 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪ Oh, pour some ♪♪

00:02:57.310 --> 00:02:59.245 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, that kind of --
[ Laughter ]

00:02:59.245 --> 00:03:02.649
And I have a big regret that
I didn't actually record this

00:03:02.649 --> 00:03:06.085
for Adam McKay, because I would
often torture him with

00:03:06.085 --> 00:03:08.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
Lynne Cheney
sings hits from the '80s.

00:03:08.254 --> 00:03:08.655 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:03:08.655 --> 00:03:12.559 align:start size:94% position:6%
Adam McKay, of course,
is the director of this film.

00:03:12.559 --> 00:03:16.596
Director of, among other films,
"The Big Short."

00:03:16.596 --> 00:03:17.030 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:20.233
-This is a case where he is
making a movie about someone

00:03:20.233 --> 00:03:23.269 align:start size:94% position:6%
whose politics
are divergent from his.

00:03:23.269 --> 00:03:23.703 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:03:23.703 --> 00:03:26.539
-Were there times -- I have
heard that you would actually

00:03:26.539 --> 00:03:29.342 align:start size:94% position:6%
argue with Adam on set
as Lynne Cheney.

00:03:29.342 --> 00:03:30.810 line:92%
-As Lynne Cheney. Adam --

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:31.444 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Light laughter ]

00:03:31.444 --> 00:03:34.480
I had a good -- I had a fun time
playing Lynne Cheney.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:35.014 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:35.014 --> 00:03:39.152
But she -- Adam likes to do
a lot of improv at times.

00:03:39.152 --> 00:03:42.488
And so to stay loose I would
kind of come and just then

00:03:42.488 --> 00:03:47.327
argue with him and criticize him
as Lynne Cheney.

00:03:47.327 --> 00:03:48.161 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:48.161 --> 00:03:50.496
Which is so not my personality,
but I would be like,

00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:55.301
"You're wearing shorts and you
want me to take you seriously

00:03:55.301 --> 00:03:57.637 size:88% position:44% line:92%
as an authority figure."

00:03:57.637 --> 00:03:59.973 size:84% position:42% line:92%
And that sort of thing.

00:03:59.973 --> 00:04:02.976 align:start size:94% position:6%
I accused him
of being a socialist.

00:04:02.976 --> 00:04:03.509 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:03.509 --> 00:04:04.877 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-That sort of thing.

00:04:04.877 --> 00:04:07.680
-It seems like --
-You know, light-hearted banter.

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:10.617 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like "how can I respect you"
kind of thing.

00:04:10.617 --> 00:04:11.184 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes, exactly.

00:04:11.184 --> 00:04:13.286 align:start size:94% position:6%
It seemed like
light-hearted banter

00:04:13.286 --> 00:04:16.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
might have been
an even more important thing

00:04:16.089 --> 00:04:18.124 align:start size:94% position:6%
to bring to "Sharp Objects."
-Yeah.

00:04:18.124 --> 00:04:22.362
-This is a very --
I mean, it's a wonderful series.

00:04:22.362 --> 00:04:24.597 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it's very dark
subject matter.

00:04:24.597 --> 00:04:25.031 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:04:25.031 --> 00:04:26.165 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You weren't just
the star of it.

00:04:26.165 --> 00:04:26.933 line:92%
You were a producer of it.

00:04:26.933 --> 00:04:29.636 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you feel as though it was
your responsibility

00:04:29.636 --> 00:04:31.004 line:92%
to try to bring levity to set?

00:04:31.004 --> 00:04:32.005 line:92%
-I did. You know, it's something

00:04:32.005 --> 00:04:34.540 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's really important to me
on set anyway.

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:35.275 size:81% position:41% line:92%
Not at the wrong time,

00:04:35.275 --> 00:04:36.943 align:start size:94% position:6%
like someone's trying to do
something serious

00:04:36.943 --> 00:04:39.412
and I'm, like, tap dancing,
you know, on their coverage.

00:04:39.412 --> 00:04:42.181
But when we have time and to
lighten it, I'd like to do that.

00:04:42.181 --> 00:04:44.717 align:start size:94% position:6%
I got an ice cream truck
for people on "Sharp Objects."

00:04:44.717 --> 00:04:50.690 size:88% position:44%
And then I also brought
a fart machine onto set.

00:04:50.690 --> 00:04:51.791 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:51.791 --> 00:04:54.661
I didn't make anybody else look
like they were doing it.

00:04:54.661 --> 00:04:56.129 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was always me.
-Gotcha. Yeah.

00:04:56.129 --> 00:04:58.197 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I didn't --
That would be fun though.

00:04:58.197 --> 00:04:58.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Next time.

00:04:58.965 --> 00:05:01.534
-Yeah, like a ventriloquist
fart machine that can throw it.

00:05:01.534 --> 00:05:03.303
-Exactly. That would be amazing.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:03.303 --> 00:05:06.172
But like a remote control so it
comes from across the room.

00:05:06.172 --> 00:05:08.174 size:81% position:41%
-Put a laser pointer
on someone else's butt

00:05:08.174 --> 00:05:10.176 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then it knows exactly
where to throw it.

00:05:10.176 --> 00:05:12.145 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Where you want it to go.
That would be great.

00:05:12.145 --> 00:05:14.681 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, we got to invent this.
-This could be so fun.

00:05:14.681 --> 00:05:16.783 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We're going to make
so much money.

00:05:16.783 --> 00:05:18.384 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-So much money.

